<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Folketing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Folketing is the parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. Created by the constitution of 1849 as the lower chamber of the Rigsdag, it became the only chamber in 1953. Since the change of system in 1901 Danish governments have needed its confidence. It has 179 members, including two each from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faroe-islands">Faroe Islands</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a>, and meets at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osu-castle">Christiansborg</a> Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/folketing.jpg" alt="Folketing" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Parliament of Denmark, Folketinget / Kontrapunkt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2018_Seal_of_the_Folketing_of_Denmark.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
